## 16. AgentDojo: A Dynamic Environment to Evaluate Prompt Injection Attacks and Defenses for LLM Agents

**Year:** 2024

**Relevance:**
Provides an environment for testing prompt injection attacks and defenses in tool-using LLM agents.

**Paper:**
https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.13352

---

## 17. Sycophancy to Subterfuge: Investigating Reward-Tampering in Language Models

**Authors:** Anthropic researchers

**Year:** 2024

**Relevance:**
Investigates whether models can generalize from simple specification gaming to more serious reward-tampering behaviors. Reward tampering is highly relevant to objective misinterpretation.

**Research:**
https://www.anthropic.com/research/reward-tampering

---

## 18. Reward Hacking in Language Model Agents: Revisiting AI Safety Gridworlds

**Authors:** Ömer Veysel Çağatan, Xuandong Zhao

**Year:** 2026

**Relevance:**
Investigates reward hacking in language-model agents using environments inspired by AI Safety Gridworlds. The work is directly related to proxy objectives and specification gaming in language-based agents.

**Paper:**
https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.15385

---

## 19. On the Generalization of Representations in Reinforcement Learning

**Authors:** Charline Le Lan, Stephen Tu, Adam Oberman, Rishabh Agarwal, Marc G. Bellemare

**Year:** 2022

**Venue:** AISTATS 2022

**Relevance:**
Studies how learned representations generalize to new states. Understanding generalization is important for analyzing why an agent can behave correctly during training but incorrectly in deployment.

**Paper:**
https://proceedings.mlr.press/v151/le-lan22a.html

