# Citation Usage

These references should be used as supporting sources for the research paper in the `paper/` directory.

When citing a paper in the research paper, the citation should correspond to the actual claim being made. For example:

> Goal misgeneralization occurs when an agent retains its capabilities while pursuing an unintended goal outside the training distribution. [1]

The corresponding reference should identify the original paper and provide its official publication link.

All research claims should be checked against the original source before final submission.
